abstract: |
  EVID-DGC is a forensic-grade, court-ready blockchain-based digital evidence management system 
  designed for law enforcement, forensic analysts, legal professionals, and judicial bodies. 
  The system leverages Polygon blockchain for immutable evidence anchoring, IPFS for decentralized 
  storage, and Supabase for secure database management. It implements an 8-role role-based access 
  control (RBAC) system, dual authentication (MetaMask wallet + Email/Password), real-time 
  notifications via Socket.IO, and comprehensive audit logging. EVID-DGC ensures the highest 
  standards of digital forensic integrity through cryptographic verification, zero-trust 
  architecture, and tamper-proof chain of custody tracking. The system is production-ready with 
  Phase 1 (Core System) and Phase 2 (Blockchain & IPFS Integration) complete, and Phase 3 
  (Advanced Forensics with AI-powered detection) in active development.
